--- Summary ---
Methods A (tool use) and B (virtual filesystem) pass consistently and
cleanly with solar-pro4 across every attempt above. Method C (named
subagent delegation — a heavier, nested multi-call path) hit persistent
429 rate-limit errors, even on a solo retry with no other case running
concurrently. This is consistent with this repo's own documented Tier-0
capacity pattern (see PLAN.md's Case 05, Finding 4: multi-round-trip
agentic calls can exceed the shared account's per-minute budget) after a
day of heavy cumulative testing across all 8 cases plus the proxy setup,
not a solar-pro4-specific defect: Methods A/B (single-round-trip calls)
never failed.
